# Three 48x48 cells in a row on a 192x64 canvas, left to right at x 32, 96 and 160. Each cell is a badge from lib/badge.ramo, a rounded plate with a round gem, drawn with the library's own p. colors. Cell 3 is two half-size badges side by side.
# Cell 1: badge with the manifest palette. A blue plate with a darker blue outline and a gold gem.
# Cell 2: the same badge with palette:forest. The plate is green with a darker green outline and the gem is red. No blue or gold remains.
# Cell 3: twin palette:forest. The left half-size badge is green with a red gem, like cell 2. The right half-size badge sets its own palette:ember inside, so it is a magenta plate with an indigo gem and nothing green or red.
# The second image, palette_key_target.png, has palette:forest on its @target and draws the same file, so cell 1 turns green with a red gem like cell 2. Cell 2 and cell 3 match the first image.
@target color/palette_key.png 192x64
@target color/palette_key_target.png 192x64 palette:forest

use badge { badge twin }

palette forest
  ramp blue #5fb05a 5
  ramp gold #e0574f 5

badge at:32,32 name:plain
badge at:96,32 palette:forest name:swapped
twin at:160,32 palette:forest name:nested
